      "title": "Grid categories need an explicit decision rule",
      "quote": "At selection ratio 8 and 20 verified outcomes, weighting had lower regret than pairing in 44 grid environments, higher regret in 22, and a difference within the prespecified tolerance in 15. At selection ratio 8 and 500 verified outcomes, weighting had lower regret than pairing in 36 grid environments, higher regret in 9, and a difference within the prespecified tolerance in 36.",
      "feedback": "I initially read “lower regret” as including every negative difference, including small differences within the tolerance. The counts sum to 81 at each budget, so the intended categories must be mutually exclusive. That resolves the arithmetic, but the passage does not say where the tolerance enters the classification. This matters especially at 500 labels, where 36 environments fall in that category. Add “Writing Δ for weighted minus paired regret and δ for the prespecified tolerance, the categories are Δ < −δ, |Δ| ≤ δ, and Δ > δ” after the second quoted sentence to state the rule used for these counts.",
      "status": "Pending",
      "severity": "minor",
      "confidence": "high"
    }
  ]
}

